    "judgment": {
      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. The first five use cosine addition or subtraction: cos(195°)=-(sqrt(2)+sqrt(6))/4; cos(x−30°)=(sqrt(3)cos x+sin x)/2; cos(x+30°)=(sqrt(3)cos x−sin x)/2; cos(x+3π/4)=−sqrt(2)(cos x+sin x)/2; cos(x−π/3)=(cos x+sqrt(3)sin x)/2. For q-170499, multiplying the complex conjugates gives 49t^12−9i^2=49t^12+9. For q-88918, 27 of 63 pets were vaccinated, giving 3/7. For q-122299, 50 of the remaining 102 cards are red, giving 25/51. For q-89040, 0.62(0.42)+0.55(0.58)=0.5794, rounding to 0.579. For q-89027, (1/3)(3/4)+(3/5)(1/4)=2/5. For q-89051, solving 2/3=3/5+p/5 gives p=1/3; the source prose mistakenly writes D′ once instead of A′, but its equations and final answer are correct. For q-89044, solving 0.36=0.12+0.60p gives 0.40. For q-6834, a=−3, b=2, c=0, so a−b+c=−5. For q-123783, eliminating t gives y=(1−x)/2 with −5≤x≤7, matching option 1. For q-16189, eliminating t gives y=(x+2)^2+1 with −6≤x≤2, matching option 0. Each source graph includes sample-point markers, while its matching choice shows the same continuous curve without those markers. For q-10752, the tangent slope is 30, its equation is y=30x−52, and its x-intercept is (26/15,0). No submitted grades were supplied; all MA evidence below comes from the respective worked solutions.",
